---
version: 2.0.2
title: testing: an invalid rule set fails the run
file: ./test/grice/testing_test.gleam
test_name: an_invalid_rule_set_fails_the_run_test
---
error[grice/invalid-rule]: Invalid rule code

A rule has the code "fixture/No-echo", which isn't a valid rule code. Codes
name rules in `gleam.toml`, so they follow a fixed syntax.

Hint: A rule code is a package-style prefix, a slash and a kebab-case name,
such as `my_app/no-io-in-view`. The prefix is a lowercase letter followed
by lowercase letters, digits and underscores, and the name is words of
lowercase letters and digits joined by single hyphens, starting with a
letter.

error[grice/invalid-config]: Unknown rule in `gleam.toml`

`rules` in entry 1 of `tools.grice.ignore` in `gleam.toml` names the rule
`fixture/no-ecko`, but no rule of this run has that code. An ignore that
names no rule silences nothing, so it's most likely a typo or a rule that
was removed.

Hint: Fix the code, or remove it from the list.

grice couldn't complete the run. Fix the problems above and run it again.

